# OpenChime daemon configuration.
#
# The daemon is configured entirely from its environment (ARCH-26); this is
# the EnvironmentFile systemd hands it. Every setting an operator may make
# is here, at its default, commented; uncomment to change one. A value that
# does not parse or is out of range stops the daemon: test an edit with
#   openchimed --check-config --env-file /etc/openchime/openchimed.env
# docs/CONFIG.md explains each. Generated by `openchimed --config-env`.
#
# This file is a package conffile: your edits survive an upgrade.

# --- Settings ---
# What the box is for: `normal` (a deployment), `development` (the tests and harnesses; the only mode that reads the Development rows) or `demo` (the public demo workspace).
#OPENCHIME_MODE=normal
# Who may notify a whole large channel with `@channel`, `@everyone` or `@here` (REQ-221): `everyone`, `admins` (owners and admins) or `nobody`. From anyone else the mention stays in the message as text and notifies nobody.
#OPENCHIME_BROADCAST_MENTIONS=everyone
# The member count from which a channel is large for `OPENCHIME_BROADCAST_MENTIONS`; 0 makes every channel large. At most 500, the most members a channel's member list carries, so a client counts a channel as the daemon does.
#OPENCHIME_BROADCAST_LARGE=0
# The welcome each new member is sent once, as a direct message from the workspace, when their account is made: the text as it is then, in the message formatting (MARKDOWN.md), `\n` for a line break. Empty: none is sent.
#OPENCHIME_WELCOME_MESSAGE=
# The public channel the workspace posts in when a new member joins, naming them. Empty: none is posted. A name that is no public, unarchived channel is said once at start, and nothing is posted.
#OPENCHIME_NOTICE_MEMBER_JOINED=
# The public channel the workspace posts in when a public channel is created, naming it and who made it. Empty: none is posted.
#OPENCHIME_NOTICE_CHANNEL_CREATED=
# Whether the workspace posts in a channel when its name, description, visibility or archived state changes, naming who changed it.
#OPENCHIME_NOTICE_CHANNEL_CHANGES=off
# The quiet hours a member follows until they set their own (REQ-136): `everyday` or `weekdays`, a space, and the hours notifications are allowed, `HH:MM-HH:MM` in each member's own time, as in `weekdays 09:00-18:00`. Empty: none, and a member without their own is never quiet.
#OPENCHIME_DEFAULT_QUIET_HOURS=
# Whether members see who has read a message (seen-by, REQ-090): `on`, or `off`, when no member's read position reaches anyone else. Each member may also stop sharing their own. Turned back on, reads from while it was off are never shown.
#OPENCHIME_READ_RECEIPTS=on
# The workspace's display name, shown to clients; unset, a client derives one from the host.
#OPENCHIME_WORKSPACE_NAME=
# Who may add a custom emoji (REQ-072): `everyone`, or `admins` (owners and admins). Deleting stays the emoji's creator's, an admin's or an owner's.
#OPENCHIME_CUSTOM_EMOJI_ADD=everyone
# How long an author may edit their own message (REQ-051): `never`, or seconds after sending, 1 to 31536000. Empty: always.
#OPENCHIME_EDIT_WINDOW=
# How long an author may delete their own message (REQ-052): `never`, or seconds after sending, 1 to 31536000. Empty: always. An admin's or owner's delete of someone else's message is never limited.
#OPENCHIME_DELETE_WINDOW=
# Public channels, by name and comma-separated, that a new member joins when their account is made, beside #general. A name that matches no public, unarchived channel is skipped, said once in the log at start.
#OPENCHIME_DEFAULT_CHANNELS=
# The most bytes one video message may hold (REQ-164), at most the attachment cap of 209715200; clients learn it at sign-in and record within it. 160 MiB by default.
#OPENCHIME_MAX_VIDEO_SIZE=167772160
# Where the daemon keeps everything: `openchime.db`, `identity/`, `blobs/`, `cert.pem`, `key.pem`, `summary/`. The packages set `/var/lib/openchime`.
OPENCHIME_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/openchime
# The TLS port the protocol, the web client and the sign-in pages are served on, and the UDP port calls use (443 for a real deployment, ARCH-54).
#OPENCHIME_PORT=8443
# The plaintext port for `/healthz` and the landing page (ARCH-25); 0 opens none.
#OPENCHIME_HEALTH_PORT=8080
# Who may join by signing in through a provider: `domain:`, `tenant:`, `subject:` and `owner:` rules, comma-separated (AUTH.md §8.4). Unset: only by invitation.
#OPENCHIME_JOIN=
# A direct connection to your own provider, 1 to 4 (SSO.md): `label=…;issuer=https://…;client_id=…;secret_file=…;subject=sub|oid;redirect=127.0.0.1|localhost`.
#OPENCHIME_OIDC_CONNECT_1=
# PEM roots the daemon trusts beside the built-in ones for its own outbound connections (push, enrollment, unfurls, S3): a service behind a private CA. No client reads it: a client trusts a private CA only through the operating system's store.
#OPENCHIME_EXTRA_CA=
# Addresses or CIDRs whose PROXY protocol v2 header is believed, comma-separated; the connection's address is then the one the proxy saw.
#OPENCHIME_TRUSTED_PROXIES=

# --- Features ---
# The certificate the daemon presents (TLS.md): `self` (its own, made at first run), `file` (`cert.pem` and `key.pem` in the data directory), `acme:<names>[;email=…][;directory=…]` (RFC 8555 for the comma-separated names), or `central` (through central; the default on a managed box).
#OPENCHIME_TLS=self
# Where accounts come from: `local` (passwords held here), `relay` (sign-in through the central service this box is enrolled with, ARCH-56), or `local,relay`.
#OPENCHIME_AUTH=local
# Whether local accounts are asked for a second step (AUTH.md §8.6).
#OPENCHIME_MFA=optional
# Attachments in S3, with `blobs/` under the data directory as their disk cache (ARCH-70): `s3://KEY:SECRET@host[:port]/bucket[/prefix][?region=…]`, or `http+s3://` for a plaintext endpoint; percent-encode `/`, `+` and `@` in the key and secret. Uploads are accepted onto the disk and sent to S3 in the background, retried until it takes them; the cache keeps to half the free space above the low-space point. A prefix puts the keys under it, so several daemons can share a bucket. Unset: local disk.
#OPENCHIME_S3=
# `OPENCHIME_S3`'s value, read from this file instead (mode 0600; a trailing newline is ignored), so the key and secret are not in the environment. Set one or the other, not both.
#OPENCHIME_S3_FILE=
# Read-aloud (ARCH-111), in a build that carries it; off saves the voice model's memory.
#OPENCHIME_TTS=on
# Voice input (ARCH-112), in a build that carries it.
#OPENCHIME_STT=on
# Summaries (REQ-310): `off`, `local` (the model runs inside the daemon, fetched on first start), or `cloud:<url>,<model>` (a hosted API's base URL and the model there).
#OPENCHIME_SUMMARY=off
# The hosted API's key, for `cloud`.
#OPENCHIME_SUMMARY_API_KEY=
# Connects this box to the OpenChime services at this origin (ARCH-84); each service is then turned on by its own setting. https, or http to loopback for a test. Prints an `oce1.` code to the log on first run.
#OPENCHIME_ENROLL_URL=
# Whether mobile push (ARCH-16/85), contentless, goes through the OpenChime services at the connection's origin; needs OPENCHIME_ENROLL_URL.
#OPENCHIME_PUSH=off
# Where push goes instead of the connection's origin; set alone, it turns push on. https, or http to loopback for a test.
#OPENCHIME_PUSH_URL=
# Whether invitations bound to an address are reported to central for it to mail (REQ-280); needs an active enrollment.
#OPENCHIME_INVITE_MAIL=off
